<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Nov trade surplus widens to $23.1 bln.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Nov trade surplus widens to $23.1 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $23.1 billion in the first 11 months of this year after a $22.4 billion surplus in the same period of 1995, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Excluding trade with other members of CIS</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Nov 96  Jan-Oct 96  Jan-Nov 95</p>
<p>    exports			    63.9	  57.7	   59.2</p>
<p>    imports			    40.8	  36.6	   36.8</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +23.1	 +21.1	  +22.4</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Nov 96  Jan-Oct 96  Jan-Nov 95</p>
<p>    exports			    80.3	  72.6	  72.1</p>
<p>    imports			    58.1	  52.3	  51.3</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +22.2	 +20.3	 +20.8</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB. Data for January-November this year are preliminary and can be revised.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
